From eb4ce0c6c086656660f2667ed9105712d3970b3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:11:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add Unit batch-6 remaining six data planes

Add the remaining six batch-6 Units on top of the 22-layer canonical tree.
No guest evidence; all six stay planned. Crypto uses deterministic test
vectors only, and the RF/network/biometric boundaries are explicit.

- unit-id (U124): US_ATECC608B at 0x35 with the 0x03 command framing and
  CRC16 (poly 0x8005) response format; INFO revision/serial, RANDOM, SHA,
  GEN_KEY, SIGN and NONCE return fixed non-secret test vectors. Real
  ECDSA/AES/Trust&GO certificate chains, key-slot locking and the 10Kb
  EEPROM are NOT modeled and NO real keys/certificates exist in the tree.
- thermal2 (U149): US_THERMAL2 at 0x32 with the ESP32 MCU register file
  (config/alarm/threshold/buzzer/RGB), derived median/average/differential
  temperatures and the 768x2B temperature array (raw = temp*128 + 8192 per
  the driver decode). The page's 0x33 address ambiguity is a blocker
  (0x33 collides with the registered thermal model); only 0x32 is modeled.
- qrcode (U173): US_QRCODE at 0x21 with the 2-byte little-endian address
  window, status/length/trigger/button/firmware/address registers and the
  0x1000-0x11FF QR data buffer. Camera/optics/decoding are NOT modeled and
  only the I2C side of the side-switch is implemented.
- uwb (U100), dmx (U183) and finger (U008): the shared UART fixture
  responder path (TX capture + idle-time response injection) with no
  protocol decoding claimed. UWB RF/ranging, DMX512/RS485 electrical
  behavior and FPC1020A fingerprint capture/matching are NOT modeled.

Offline QOM smoke (S3 board, no guest firmware) validates property
registration, fixtures, range/read-only rejection and the responder
fixtures; it is not a functional PASS.
